meta {
  name: Course sim route (shape)
  type: http
  seq: 17
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/courses/:id/sim-route
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:path {
  id: 35
}

params:query {
  roundingM: 30
}

docs {
  200 { courseId, name, version, builtinKey, roundingM, key, cached, shape:{marks,startLine,finishLine}, wps:[{x,y,kind,side?,ref?}] }
  404 { error }

  The scripted route compiled on the course SHAPE (todo 32), in wind-frame
  metres (x = east, y = upwind) and NOT placed on the water: start line
  centre, then every mark already offset `roundingM` metres to its
  required side (gates collapsed to a crossing point near the first buoy),
  then the finish centre. A session only rotates / scales / translates
  this list onto its own origin and wind.

  `key` is a hash of the shape; it is what makes the stored route
  self-invalidating. `cached: true` means it came off the course row
  (compiled once, reused); false means it was compiled for this call and
  stored. Editing a course changes the shape, hence the key, hence a
  recompile — there is nothing to invalidate by hand.

  `?roundingM=` recompiles at another pass distance (5..200, default 30).
  Reading a built-in is fine and nothing here needs write access: the
  compiled route is stored on the course row as server bookkeeping, and on
  a built-in only that cache column is ever touched.

  Same source as tools/draw-routes.js, which draws one figure per course
  so the route can be checked by eye.
}
